  "plain": "Maaneli Derakhshani, speaking on Jesse Michels's podcast, says that a trio of lights seen in photographs from Apollo 17, a later NASA mission to the Moon, also shows up in footage from Apollo 11, the 1969 mission that first landed people on the Moon. He points to the repetition across missions as a sign that something unexplained was there, rather than a one-off flaw in a single picture."
